3. The helper method is private since it's only used within this test class
4. All the test assertions remain the same, just moved to a more reusable location
5. The test method is now more focused on its single responsibility of testing static method hiding

This improves:
- Code reusability (can be used by other test methods)
- Readability (test method is more concise)
- Maintainability (verification logic is in one place)
- Modularity (separates setup from verification)

