2. The helper method handles the common case of verifying method order in top-down hierarchy
3. The test method now uses this helper for the common cases and keeps the special cases as direct assertions
4. The helper method dynamically determines the method names based on the predicate and expected classes

This reduces code duplication while maintaining the same test coverage and making the test method more readable. The helper method could be reused by other tests that need to verify method ordering in top-down hierarchy traversal.

