I'll extract the common logic of creating and running the console launcher into a separate method. Here's the refactored code:

##########################
@ParameterizedTest(name = "{0}")
@MethodSource("commandsWithEmptyOptionExitCodes")
void disableBanner(String command, int expectedExitCode) {
    var exitCode = runConsoleLauncher(command, "--disable-banner").getExitCode();

    assertEquals(expectedExitCode, exitCode);
    assertThat(stringWriter.toString()).doesNotContain("Thanks for using JUnit!");
}

private ConsoleLauncherExecutionResult runConsoleLauncher(String... args) {
    var consoleLauncher = new ConsoleLauncher(ConsoleTestExecutor::new, printSink, printSink);
    return consoleLauncher.run(args);
}
##########################

Note: I also created a suggestion for the return type (`ConsoleLauncherExecutionResult`) which would be the type returned by `consoleLauncher.run()`. The exact type name might need to be adjusted based on the actual return type in the codebase.

